dwarfdump --print-debug-gnu: name without a NUL in the
last .debug_gnu_pubnames entry reads past the section
(heap over-read)
 #346


If the last name in a .debug_gnu_pubnames block has
no NUL inside the block's entry area, and the 4-byte
end-of-block word (which should be zero) is not zero,
dwarfdump --print-debug-gnu prints the name with a string
scan that runs off the end of the section buffer. Here is
a 27-byte section with one block and one entry:

(unit_length 0x17, version 2, CU offset 0, CU size 0,
then one entry: DIE offset 0x0b, flag 0x30, the name
"main" with no NUL. The end-of-block word is "YYYY".)

The release build exits 0 and prints the name together
with the end-of-block word and whatever bytes follow the
section in memory. ASan build:


